WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.190
Three receipts from a
stationery shop: pens,

2
00:00:03.240 --> 00:00:05.180
notebooks and folders.

3
00:00:05.230 --> 00:00:10.320
Three pens, two notebooks, one
folder: twelve pounds forty.

4
00:00:10.370 --> 00:00:15.100
One pen, four notebooks, two
folders: eighteen eighty.

5
00:00:15.150 --> 00:00:20.010
Five pens, one notebook, three
folders: nineteen ninety.

6
00:00:20.060 --> 00:00:22.200
Not one price is printed.

7
00:00:22.250 --> 00:00:23.860
Do you divide by something?

8
00:00:23.910 --> 00:00:25.470
Guess until it fits?

9
00:00:25.520 --> 00:00:28.480
Or can one matrix find every price?

10
00:00:28.530 --> 00:00:32.130
In this mission, you'll treat a
matrix as a grid with an order,

11
00:00:32.180 --> 00:00:33.770
rows by columns.

12
00:00:33.820 --> 00:00:36.380
These quantities make a three by three.

13
00:00:36.430 --> 00:00:40.200
You'll multiply a matrix
by a column, row by column.

14
00:00:40.250 --> 00:00:43.930
Row one times the unknown
prices gives the first total.

15
00:00:43.980 --> 00:00:46.880
And all three receipts
become one equation:

16
00:00:46.930 --> 00:00:48.980
A x equals b.

17
00:00:49.030 --> 00:00:53.550
Your mission: work out how one
matrix finds all three prices.
